  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat percentage of Faraday's flower-shop sales came from sunflower bouquets? Faraday owns a flower stall. Faraday's flower shop sold 50 bouquets during the week. 12 of the bouquets sold that week were sunflower bouquets.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "LOSSY SELF-SUMMARY; VERIFY AGAINST NEW INPUTS\nVISIBLE PREFIX THROUGH TURN 6; LOSSY EXTRACT:\n- {\"content\":\"Good, now using that, can you calculate: How many sunflowers was Faraday able to sell after three days? And here are a few things you should know: Faraday sells bouquets of sunflowers for $8 each. Faraday earns $26 per day fr...\n- {\"content\":\"Faraday earns **$26 per day** from individual sunflowers. Over 3 days:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n26 \\\\times 3 = \\\\$78\\n\\\\]\\n\\nSince each individual sunflower sells for $3:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\frac{78}{3}=26\\n\\\\]\\n\\nTherefore, Faraday sold:\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\box...\n- {\"content\":\"One more thing — Each bouquet contains 12 sunflowers.\",\"role\":\"user\"}\n- {\"content\":\"Over 3 days:\\n\\n**Individual sunflowers:**\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\$26 \\\\times 3=\\\\$78\\n\\\\]\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\$78 \\\\div \\\\$3=26\\\\text{ individual sunflowers}\\n\\\\]\\n\\n**Sunflowers in bouquets:**\\n\\n\\\\[\\n\\\\$56\\\\div \\\\$8=7\\\\text{ bouquets per day}\\n\\...",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Faraday sells individual sunflowers for $2 each.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Faraday sold 12 sunflower bouquets out of 50 total bouquets.\n\n\\[\n\\text{Percentage}=\\frac{12}{50}\\times 100\\%=24\\%\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{24\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
